%S A399359 1,24,1224,80160,5949000,475905024,40024355616,3488577054336,
%T A399359 312328831062600,28551491753928000,2653919421153796224,
%U A399359 250075962042564243456,23833826950179627422496,2293472314608867448680960,222522632590147008937257600,21744945220565852074845596160
%N A399359 a(n) = 108^n * [z^n] hypergeom([1/6, 1/3], [1], z)^4.
%C A399359 Fourth-power coefficient sequence at the mixed cubic CM point (1/6,1/3;1). This is the self-convolution of A184423.
%C A399359 For every prime p >= 5 and all positive integers m,r, the paper in Links proves a(m*p^r) == a(m*p^(r-1)) (mod p^(3*r)).
%C A399359 The exponent 3*r is best possible uniformly: a(7)-a(1) = 3488577054312 = 7^3*10170778584, where 7 does not divide 10170778584.
%H A399359 Alex Shvets, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21856818">Sharp Prime-Power Supercongruences for the Even Powers at the Mixed Cubic CM Point</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%F A399359 G.f.: Sum_{n>=0} a(n)*x^n = hypergeom([1/6,1/3],[1],108*x)^4.
%F A399359 a(n) = Sum_{k=0..n} A184423(k)*A184423(n-k).
%F A399359 a(n) = Sum_{k=0..n} (3*k)!*(2*k)!*(3*(n-k))!*(2*(n-k))!/((k!)^5*((n-k)!)^5).
%F A399359 n^5*a(n) = 6*(2*n-1)*(18*n^4-36*n^3+37*n^2-19*n+4)*a(n-1) - 36*(n-1)*(3*n-4)*(3*n-2)*(6*n-7)*(6*n-5)*a(n-2) for n >= 2, with a(0) = 1 and a(1) = 24.
%F A399359 a(n) ~ 2^(2*n - 14/3) * 3^(3*n + 5/2) * Gamma(1/3)^6 / (Pi^(11/2) * n^(3/2)). - _Vaclav Kotesovec_, Aug 28 2026
%e A399359 a(2) = 1*540 + 12*12 + 540*1 = 1224 (from convolution formula).
%t A399359 Table[Sum[(3*k)! * (2*k)! * (3*(n-k))! * (2*(n-k))! / (k!^5 * (n-k)!^5), {k, 0, n}], {n, 0, 20}] (* _Vaclav Kotesovec_, Aug 28 2026 *)
%o A399359 (PARI) a(n) = sum(k=0, n, (3*k)!*(2*k)!*(3*(n-k))!*(2*(n-k))!/((k!)^5*((n-k)!)^5))
%Y A399359 Cf. A184423, A393983, A397472.
%K A399359 nonn,easy,new
%O A399359 0,2
%A A399359 _Alex Shvets_, Aug 26 2026
